        *Demo gif (may take a moment to load)*

        ## Dependencies

        - **Required**: BepInEx 5, PEAKLib.Core, PEAKLib.UI, ModConfig 1.8.1
        - **Optional**: XUnity AutoTranslator (untranslated check / original-text toggle / reload / dictionary mirroring — the related buttons stay greyed out without it), TimeTheme (day/night palette)
        - **Conflicts**: LocalFix < 2.17.0 ships the same patch set, so this mod refuses to attach when it's detected; the patches also skip automatically when the ModSettingsLocalization fork (a ModConfig 1.6.0 variant) is present.

        ## Language files

        Directory: `BepInEx\config\ModConfigEnhance\language\`

        File format is identical to XUnity dictionaries: `key=translation`, `//` comments, `\n` newline, `\=` literal equals, `{0}` `{1}` placeholders kept — **never modify anything left of `=`** (it is the key the dictionary matches character-for-character against on-screen text). The first `MCE_…=…` block is this mod's UI terms (stable IDs — translate the right side only); the `original=translation` lines after it are handed to XUnity AutoTranslator.

        Files starting with `_` stay out of the dropdown; only the top-level `.txt` files are read — keep backups in a subfolder.

        ### File naming: `language-code[-variant][_part].txt`

        The filename itself decides its group and how it's displayed — the two suffixes do different jobs:

        | Pattern | Meaning | Examples |
        |---|---|---|
        | `code.txt` | Base group for the language | `zh-cn.txt`, `en-us.txt` |
        | `code-variant.txt` | **Standalone group of the same language code** — a full, independent translation that may use a completely different style | `zh-cn-old.txt`, `zh-cn-memes.txt` |
        | `group_part.txt` | **Sub-file of a group** — merged into the group named before the `_`, loaded after it in filename order, later entries win | `zh-cn_topup.txt`, `zh-cn-old_fix.txt` |

        - **Language code** = the leading `xx` or `xx-yy` of the filename (`zh-cn-old` → `zh-cn`). It only governs two things: the XUnity mirror folder (`Translation\<code>`) and "Follow game language" matching. Aliases: `zh`=`zh-cn`, `en`=`en-us`.
        - **Dropdown label**: a `// display: <name>` first line shows `name (filename)`; without it, the plain filename is shown. Groups with more than one file get `×count` appended. Examples: `zh-cn-old.txt` (with `// display: Old translation`) → `Old translation (zh-cn-old)`; `zh-cn.txt` (none) → `zh-cn`; `zh-cn-basic.txt` (`// display: 简体中文`) + `zh-cn-basic_ModB.txt` → `简体中文 (zh-cn-basic) ×2`.
        - **Loaded-files list**: after picking a group, the panel lists each file with its own display name, e.g. `zh-cn-basic.txt (简体中文)`, `zh-cn-basic_ModB.txt (Modb)`.
        - **Tooltip emphasis**: in `MCE_TIP_*` hover-tooltips, text inside `` `…` `` or `“…”` renders in the title color (backticks hidden, curly quotes kept).
        - **Variant groups are independent**: same-code groups are equal, self-contained translations — the untranslated check counts only the current group, like `cn` vs `tw`.
        - **Follow game language** with several same-code groups prefers the group named exactly the code (`zh-cn`), else the first variant.

        ### Adding a language

        1. **Export** — mod settings → left column → **Export texts**; tick **Selected only** first to drop the mods you don't need (this mod is always included).
        2. **Translate** — fill the right side of each `=` following the rules inside the file; keep `\n` and `\=` notation as-is.
        3. **Rename & place** — save as UTF-8 and name by the rules above: a new language uses `lowercase-code.txt` (`de-de.txt`, `ja-jp.txt`…), an alternative style for the same language uses `code-variant.txt`; move it into `language\`. To change the dropdown label, write `// display: <name>` on the first line.
        4. **Enable** — back in the game: click **Refresh**, pick the language in the dropdown — it loads automatically. After edits, click **Reload texts**.

        ### Group sub-files & top-ups

        `group_part.txt` merges into the group named before the `_` (base file first, sub-files in filename order — text sorting, not numeric; pad sequential numbers `01`, `02`, `10`):

        ```text
        zh-cn.txt             base file
        zh-cn_01_base.txt     sub-file: appended
        zh-cn_20_topup.txt    sub-file: overrides same keys
        zh-cn-old_fix.txt     joins the zh-cn-old group, not zh-cn
        ```

        - Later files override earlier ones; identical entries are skipped; conflicting translations are logged with their source files.
        - Empty values, original-text placeholders and unchanged English `MCE_` values cannot overwrite existing translations.
        - A group is validated before applying; format errors (missing `=`, empty file…) show in the description panel in orange with line numbers — fix and reload.

        Top-up workflow: keep the old files → **Untranslated** → translate → save as a new `_part` file for the same group → **Reload texts**. The untranslated check counts only the current group's own coverage; **do not replace your full translation with a patch**. For a new language or variant group, click **Refresh** and select it.

        ### After picking a language (no restart)

        - This mod's UI switches at once; the description panel lists every loaded filename in load order (with each file's display name).
        - XUnity AutoTranslator switches to that group's language code: its dictionary folder becomes `Translation\<code>\Text\`, the translations are written there as `ModConfigEnhance_<code>.txt`, dictionaries reload, texts without a translation show the original, and `Language=` in `AutoTranslatorConfig.ini` is updated for the next start. Toggle this link with this mod's **Switch XUnity language with the language file** option.

        ## Toolbar

        | Button | What it does |
        |---|---|
        | Export texts | Exports all UI texts to `export\` (this mod's `MCE_` block + one block per mod, manifest summaries included) |
        | Untranslated | Exports only the entries the XUnity dictionary doesn't cover (requires XUnity AutoTranslator) |
        | Selected only | Adds an "Export" checkbox column to the sidebar — only the ticked mods get exported (this mod is always included) |
        | Show original / Show translated | Global original ↔ translation toggle (same as XUnity's Alt+T) |
        | Reload texts | Re-reads the language files and refreshes XUnity's dictionaries |
        | Open folder | Opens `config\ModConfigEnhance\` |
        | Language ▾ / Refresh | Pick a language group; **Refresh** after adding a new language, **Reload texts** after adding a sub-file to an existing one |

        ## Gamepad controls

        - **Navigation**: stick / D-pad moves focus; A confirms/enters; B steps back level by level (slider → editing → capture → right panel → left panel → leave page)
        - **LB/RB**: switch mods
        - **Sliders**: A arms value mode, left/right adjust, A or B exits; each step is 0.5% of the range — hold for 1s to auto-repeat at 10 steps/s, 3s for 40 steps/s
        - **Dropdowns**: A opens, up/down to move, A picks, B closes
        - **Input fields**: A starts editing, B exits. No on-screen keyboard — type on a physical keyboard or the platform OSK (Steam+X on Steam Deck)
        - **Keybinds**: A starts capture, hold the target key for 1 second to write it; B cancels

        ## Config file

        `BepInEx\config\com.aiae.modconfigenhance.cfg`:

        | Section | Contents |
        |---|---|
        | 1. Layout | Tree sidebar and description panel toggles (restart required) |
        | 2. Localization | UI localization, hide localization buttons (instant), make XUnity follow the chosen language file, disable XUnity machine translation (on by default — turn off to restore machine translation) |
        | 3. State | Runtime state: language file, pins, export exclusions etc. (Hidden) |

        ## Extra details

        - **Sidebar cascade**: reopening the settings page reveals the selected mod row first, then one row above and below per beat; at the bottom rows appear upward; with no valid selection it starts from the top. Closing ends the animation and restores pending rows.
        - **Wheel step**: the left sidebar wheel step is about a third of vanilla, with a ~0.1s ease; scrollbar dragging and controller positioning take over immediately — other scroll areas are unchanged.
        - **Description panel**: selecting a mod/section shows its name, version and manifest summary; hovering/focusing an option restores that option's description.

        ## Feedback & contribute

        `2323086800@qq.com` / QQ group `1104320838` — finished language files are welcome too; send them to AiAe and they ship with the next release.

        """;

